# React testing

`README.md` wins if this rule disagrees with it, except the commands, which match `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.

## What CI runs

From `frontend/`, on Node 20: `npm ci`, then `npm run lint`, `npx next build`, and `npm run test:coverage`.

`npm run test:coverage` is `vitest run --coverage`. The include pattern is `**/*.{test,spec}.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}` with `jsdom`, Testing Library, and `frontend/vitest.setup.tsx`. Put new tests under `frontend/__tests__/`. A bug fix adds a regression test there when the behavior is in the frontend.

Do not add Jest or a second runner. There is no numeric coverage gate. `vitest.config.ts` has reporters and no threshold. Do not add one.

`@axe-core/react` is already available for accessibility checks. Use it in the existing accessibility tests. It does not replace `npm run test:coverage`.

## How to assert

- Assert what the operator can observe or what the module returns.
- Do not assert private state, render counts, or which `use*` function ran.
- Do not snapshot whole component trees.
- Changed UI still needs `npm run lint` and `npx next build`.
